+// native-s16 op as its own single-instruction Ac16 transit. This pass does the
+// same collapse PRE-RA, on the still-SSA virtual Ac16/Imag16 vregs, so the
+// allocator instead sees ONE multi-instruction (spillable) Ac16 range threaded
+// across the dependent chain — the "residency" that Phase 3 is about. It is a
+// straight SSA RAUW: for `%lo = LDAImag16 %home` whose %home is single-def by
+// `%home = STAImag16 %src` in the same block, replace %lo with %src and drop the
+// reload (and the now-dead store). SSA single-def of %home and %src guarantees
+// the reloaded value is exactly %src — no clobber analysis needed. The 1d-
+// entanglement this RAUW would otherwise risk (an 8-bit value coalescing into
+// the widened Ac16 range) is *prevented* by the B0 shouldCoalesce barrier, which
+// is this pass's mandatory safety companion. OFF by default: measurement only.
